<!-- PROFILES -->
<section class="block" id="profiles" style="padding-top:40px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="overline">A Category Question, Not a Product Race</div>
      <h2>The data layer &mdash; and the engine built around it</h2>
      <p>The honest read from our analysis: GeoPostCodes is the reference-data supplier inside ioNova ARS. One is a dataset; the other is the compliance engine and application that already contains it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vs-grid reveal">
      <div class="card profile theirs">
        <h3>GeoPostCodes</h3>
        <div class="sub">Postal reference data vendor &middot; GeoPostCodes srl (Belgium, est. 2005)</div>
        <p class="desc">A specialist data product: self-hosted postal reference tables covering 246 countries, delivered as files and a download API &mdash; no parsing service, no inference component.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>9.3M postal codes, 4M cities, 24M streets across 84 countries, 116K UNLOCODEs.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>Weekly updates compiled from 1,500+ authoritative sources.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>Air-gapped by design &mdash; downloaded data, zero internet dependency, cannot hallucinate.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>Small private SME (~30&ndash;50 employees); no formal security certifications documented.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent profile ours">
        <h3>ioNova ARS</h3>
        <div class="sub">Financial-messaging compliance engine &middot; deterministic rules + reference data</div>
        <p class="desc">A purpose-built compliance engine &mdash; and a full application &mdash; that parses SWIFT MT free text and ISO 20022 XML, preserves financial identifiers, and emits regulator-citable corrected XML for the November 2026 mandate.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Embeds the GeoPostCodes 246-country dataset as its verification layer &mdash; plus the parsing, correction, audit and integration engine around it.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Extracts and preserves 50+ financial identifiers (BIC, IBAN, LEI, ABA&hellip;); 30 reason codes citing EPC153-22, PMPG, EU Reg 2023/1113, CBPR+.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Full application: Exceptions Workbench, live dashboards and Developer Portal &mdash; not just an engine.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Six integration mechanisms; start in days, live in 2&ndash;4 weeks; Cloud / VPC / on-prem / air-gapped.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

