<section class="block" id="application" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="app-band reveal">
      <div class="inner">
        <div style="text-align:center"><span class="overline">The Application Advantage</span></div>
        <h2>GeoPostCodes is the ingredient.<br>ioNova is the <span style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6ED9DA,#5EA1DC,#8ECDF2);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent">finished application.</span></h2>
        <p class="sub">Licensing reference data leaves the entire engine &mdash; parsing, correction, audit, review workflow, monitoring, integration &mdash; to be built. ARS ships all of it, with the same data already inside.</p>
        <div class="app-grid">
          <div class="app-card">
            <div class="icon-container ic-cyan"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 12h-6l-2 3h-4l-2-3H2"/><path d="M5.45 5.11 2 12v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6l-3.45-6.89A2 2 0 0 0 16.76 4H7.24a2 2 0 0 0-1.79 1.11Z"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Exceptions Workbench</h3>
            <p>Low-confidence resolutions route to maker-checker review queues with per-field confidence, the proposed repair and the rule citation behind it &mdash; every action audit-logged.</p>
            <div class="contrast"><b>GeoPostCodes:</b> no service component exists &mdash; review workflow is whatever the customer builds.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-card">
            <div class="icon-container ic-blue"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 12A10 10 0 1 1 12 2"/><path d="M22 2 12 12"/><path d="M16 2h6v6"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Live Dashboards</h3>
            <p>Real-time STP rate, exception ageing, latency percentiles, reason-code distribution and per-country compliance posture &mdash; examiner-ready evidence, always current.</p>
            <div class="contrast"><b>GeoPostCodes:</b> N/A &mdash; operations run on the customer&rsquo;s own infrastructure.<span style="color:var(--alert-amber)">&dagger;</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-card">
            <div class="icon-container ic-teal"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m18 16 4-4-4-4M6 8l-4 4 4 4M14.5 4l-5 16"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Developer Portal</h3>
            <p>Self-service onboarding, API keys, sandbox with SWIFT MT / ISO 20022 test corpora, OpenAPI specs and integration guides. First message parsed the day access is granted.</p>
            <div class="contrast"><b>GeoPostCodes:</b> a data download API &mdash; everything from parsing to validation is your build.<span style="color:var(--alert-amber)">&dagger;</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 style="text-align:center;color:#fff;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:18px">Six ways to integrate &mdash; versus a file download</h3>
