      <h2>What teams ask about GeoPostCodes vs <span class="grad-text">ioNova ARS</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq reveal">
      <div class="faq-item open">
        <button class="faq-q">Is GeoPostCodes a competitor to ioNova?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>No &mdash; it is ioNova&rsquo;s embedded data supplier. ARS ships with the GeoPostCodes 246-country dataset inside as its verification layer, so the two sit in the same stack, not on the same shortlist. The real procurement question is &ldquo;which problem are we solving&rdquo;: parsing-and-correction (an engine) versus reference-data enrichment (a dataset).</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">When should we license GeoPostCodes directly?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>For non-payment uses: logistics, e-commerce, ERP, GIS and market-research teams that need self-hosted global postal reference data and are prepared to build their own logic on top. For payments address compliance, the same data is already inside ARS &mdash; a direct licence adds procurement effort without adding capability.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Why does GeoPostCodes score so low in this analysis?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Because it was scored against a parser&rsquo;s job description. Twelve of the 25 &ldquo;Not Met&rdquo; results are architectural: a reference-data product cannot extract financial identifiers or produce confidence scores, because it performs no parse at all. Within its own category, the analysis calls it a high-quality offering &mdash; the low composite is a category mismatch, not a quality verdict.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Could we build our own parser on GeoPostCodes data?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes &mdash; that is the in-house path, and the data licence is the smallest line item in it. The parsing engine, financial-identifier extraction, regulator-grade audit trail and ongoing rule maintenance are an 18&ndash;36 month build with a standing engineering team behind it. ARS delivers the same outcome, on the same data, in 2&ndash;4 weeks.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Is the weekly data refresh a problem?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>For a data product, no &mdash; freshness is a feature. For a compliance system built directly on it, unpinned weekly drift breaks replayability: the same input can resolve differently after a refresh, and a regulator cannot re-run last quarter&rsquo;s decision. ARS versions both its rules and its embedded data, so identical input replays identically.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Does ioNova actually ship a UI, or is it another API?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
